## CALENDAR AUTOMATION RULES

### Auto-Schedule Principles

1. **Deadline First:** Government deadline always on calendar first
2. **Work Backwards:** Action deadlines auto-set (Gov - 5 days, - 3 days, - 1 day)
3. **Stage Gates:** Each stage transition gets a calendar slot
4. **Deep Work:** Proposals in Stage 4 get 4-hour blocks
5. **Follow-Up:** All external contacts get reminder scheduling
6. **Buffer Time:** Never schedule work right up to deadline

### Calendar Conflict Resolution

```
CONFLICT DETECTED:

Attempting to schedule: [2-hour proposal block] for [Bid A]
Conflict with: [Existing event] — [Bid B submission]

OPTIONS:
├── 1. Move [Bid A] to [Alternative time]
├── 2. Shorten [Bid A] to 1 hour (partial progress)
├── 3. Delegate: Can [Bid A] Stage advance without Dee? (NEXUS automation)
└── 4. Prioritize: Which bid has sooner deadline? (Auto-suggest)

RECOMMENDATION: [X]
```

